# CORE / PRIORITY repos — your highest-value product repos.
#
# The autonomous schedule-build PRIORITISES these over every other repo.
# Tasks for repos listed here keep their assigned priority (P0/P1/P2);
# every OTHER repo's pending tasks are capped at P3 (bottom of the queue),
# so the runner always drains your core product before secondary apps.
#
# Enforced by scripts/reprioritize_queue.sh (run at session start + wrap up).
#
# One repo name per line (task-store convention = git basename). '#' lines ignored.
#
# Example:
#   my-core-app
#   my-core-api
#
# This .example file is the fork-ready template. Copy to `schedule_priority.txt`
# and list your own core repo basenames.
